  <reason>Subject and account: The subject of this report is Fahad Zafar, holder of account PK**HABB****8796, opened on 24 December 2019. The customer's declared occupation is student, with a declared income of PKR 20,000 per month.

Activity summary: During the period 2 March 2026 to 11 March 2026, the account recorded 25 credits totalling PKR 1,236,000 as well as 5 debits totalling PKR 1,089,000. The credits arrived as 25 interbank (IBFT) transfers from 21 distinct senders. The activity was detected on 11 March 2026, when Tazama typology MULE-01 scored 360 against an alert threshold of 300.

Grounds for suspicion: The account received funds from 21 distinct senders within the activity window. Funds did not remain in the account: debits equal to 88% of credits, with a median of 7.1 hours between the latest credit and each debit. For a customer whose declared occupation is student, credits in the activity window were 61.8 times the declared monthly income, against a declared income of PKR 20,000 per month. Taken together, these indicators are consistent with suspected money mule activity; the reporting entity has not established the underlying offence.

Flow of funds: Of the outgoing funds, PKR 697,000 was sent to QuickPay wallet ***0932 (WLT****0932, Synthetic EMI) in 3 transactions. Of the outgoing funds, PKR 392,000 was withdrawn as Cash (ATM) in 2 transactions.

Other considerations: Screening of the subject returned no match on sanctions, PEP or adverse-media screening on 29 March 2026.

Action taken by the reporting entity: Action taken: a note by L2 analyst (12 March 2026): "Outgoing wallet transfers placed on hold pending review. No contact made with the customer about this review."</reason>
